# D-RPB-5 evidence-commit policy (builder's call per plan §2 / §14;
# mirrors the v2 D-PBR-5 precedent exactly — same shape, real-PB
# task ids).
#
# Reproducibility of the HEADLINE (AC.RPB.6) requires the structured
# evidence retrievable: verdict.json (the computed three-valued
# verdict + per-arm failure-signature map + measured cost + the
# agent-vs-eval-emulation wall-clock split) and the per-task
# disposition.json records ARE committed — re-running the frozen
# scorer over them yields the same verdict. The BULKY raw `claude`
# transcripts + per-(arm,task) work dirs + loop artefacts + the real
# upstream eval_run trees (incl. the large *.eval.json + the
# submission.tar.gz blobs) stay LOCAL (not committed) — mirrors the
# v0.4.0 C4 / v2 D-PBR-5 precedent of keeping raw runs out-of-tree
# without bloating the repo with raw model output + multi-MB eval
# artefacts. The structured disposition.json records carry the real
# upstream graded score + n_resolved/n_tests + error_code + the
# eval.json path, so the headline is reproducible + auditable from
# the committed records; the raw transcripts + raw eval trees are
# local-only forensic depth (the detached dispatcher-owned run owns
# them; they regenerate from the content-hash-pinned frozen set).

# bulky raw run artefacts — local only
*/baseline.transcript
*/loam.transcript
*/baseline_work/
*/loam_work/
*/loam_artifacts/
*/_frozen/
*/eval_run/
run.log
.detached_pid

# KEEP (committed, reproducibility-bearing): verdict.json,
# <task>/disposition.json, this .gitignore
!*/disposition.json
